---

## Lore

This character is the professional game hunter. He has travelled the world in
search of game and challenges in the wilderness - but the world is shrinking,
with far less wilderness and too few challenges, and recently he has turned his
attention to the deadliest game of all.

Like a true hunter he has donned the clothes that best hide him in his prey''s
environment, and goes forth to stalk. His prey is a deadly predator who kills for
pleasure and slays his own kind, a beast with many names: pusher, pimp, murderer,
crime boss, hit man, burglar, terrorist, and dozens of others, all basically the
same animal. Some would call them scavengers. That is their mistake. These are
rogue predators who feed on the weak, the helpless and the innocent, man-killers
who stalk the streets with the same ferocity as the tiger in his jungle.

There is a newcomer to the territory. A new predator, who hunts the hunters.

## GM Notes

**The hunter-related list**, printed 155-156 - seven of the fifteen, with the
one-time bonus the book prints beside each:

Archery; Biology (+10%); Climbing including rappelling (+30%); Detect Ambush
(+10%); Detect Concealment (+10%); First Aid (+20%); Fishing (+20%);
Intelligence (+20%); Prowl (+30%); Radio: Basic (+20%); Sniper; Swimming: Basic
(+30%); Swimming: Advanced (+20%); Pilot: Sailboat; Pilot: Motorboat; Pilot:
Truck.

The catalog holds one `Swimming` row rather than a basic and an advanced one, so
that pair is one entry here.

**Years of experience**, printed 156, hunting having possibly begun in
childhood: 01-17 six years, 18-35 eight, 36-52 ten, 53-69 twelve, 70-86
fourteen, 87-00 sixteen.

**The equipment budget**, printed 156: 01-15 $8,000; 16-29 $10,000; 30-45
$12,000; 46-60 $14,000; 61-75 $16,000; 76-89 $18,000; 90-00 $20,000. At least
30% must go on weapons, ammunition and accessories and 20% on camping, hunting
and wilderness equipment; up to 30% may be saved. The character presumably
already has a furnished apartment and reasonable possessions.
', 'published', 'data-script'
